      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nOn Windows, standard global or user-site Python installations place executables/scripts in a `Scripts` subdirectory (e.g., `C:\\Python311\\Scripts\\llamafactory-cli.exe`) rather than directly in the parent directory of `sys.executable`. Without a fallback check, this will raise a `FileNotFoundError` for Windows users who are not running inside a virtual environment.\n\nAdding a check for the `Scripts` directory and falling back to a bare `\"llamafactory-cli\"` search on the system `PATH` ensures robustness across all Windows installation types.\n\n```suggestion\n            if os.name == \"nt\":\n                cli_exe = str(Path(sys.executable).parent / \"llamafactory-cli.exe\")\n                if not Path(cli_exe).exists():\n                    cli_exe = str(Path(sys.executable).parent / \"Scripts\" / \"llamafactory-cli.exe\")\n                if not Path(cli_exe).exists():\n                    cli_exe = \"llamafactory-cli\"\n            else:\n                cli_exe = str(Path(sys.executable).parent / \"llamafactory-cli\")\n                if not Path(cli_exe).exists():\n                    cli_exe = \"llamafactory-cli\"\n```",
      "commit_id": "526c099e77b2745e1e825e5afaeed0f65f58cc04",
      "copilot_code_review_sources": [],
      "created_at": "2026-07-21T10:18:17Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -380,14 +382,20 @@ def _launch(self, data: dict[\"Component\", Any], do_train: bool) -> Generator[dic\n             env = deepcopy(os.environ)\n             env[\"LLAMABOARD_ENABLED\"] = \"1\"\n             env[\"LLAMABOARD_WORKDIR\"] = args[\"output_dir\"]\n+            if os.name == \"nt\":\n+                cli_exe = str(Path(sys.executable).parent / \"llamafactory-cli.exe\")\n+            else:\n+                cli_exe = str(Path(sys.executable).parent / \"llamafactory-cli\")\n+                if not Path(cli_exe).exists():\n+                    cli_exe = \"llamafactory-cli\"",
