      "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
      "body": "There is a simpler route that needs no path resolution at all: `src/llamafactory/cli.py` already ends with `if __name__ == \"__main__\": freeze_support(); main()`, so `[sys.executable, \"-m\", \"llamafactory.cli\", ...]` launches the same entry point and works for editable installs, conda envs and any Scripts layout, on every platform. That also removes the `\"llamafactory-cli\"` bare-name fallback, which silently resolves against `PATH` and can pick a different environment than the one running the WebUI.",
      "commit_id": "2da088d0a8f7e5a66c75eeacee3071e2053778ac",
      "copilot_code_review_sources": [],
      "created_at": "2026-08-29T08:34:41Z",
